  "reasoning": {
    "RA": "Sprint 1 delivered core scaffold, CF deploy, data layer, and AI/SE setups, but critical SEO foundations (llms-full.txt, JSON-LD injection, canonical tags, Open Graph/Twitter meta) are missing or unverified; these are mandatory per locked ADRs and must be fixed before Sprint 2.",
    "RB": "The deploy adapter and runtime edge cases were resolved, but Sprint 2 introduces calculator form logic and n8n integration—untouched complexity—plus the SEO foundation gaps increase risk of rework; medium confidence is prudent."
  },
  "concerns_observed": [
    {
      "title": "Missing llms-full.txt",
      "category": "seo_ai",
      "severity": "high",
      "must_fix_before_sprint_2": true,
      "description": "ADR-015 requires both llms.txt and llms-full.txt; only llms.txt was found. llms-full.txt is essential for full-context AI crawling and must be added."
    },
    {
      "title": "No evidence of JSON-LD structured data on page",
      "category": "seo_ai",
      "severity": "high",
      "must_fix_before_sprint_2": true,
      "description": "The repository includes lib/jsonld.ts but no proof it is actually injected into the rendered HTML. JSON-LD for Organization, LocalBusiness, Product, etc. is a baseline SEO contract (ADR-014). Missing this will harm rich results from day one."
    },
    {
      "title": "Self-referencing canonical tags missing",
      "category": "seo_ai",
      "severity": "high",
      "must_fix_before_sprint_2": true,
      "description": "Round 3 consensus mandated self-referencing canonical <link> tags on every page. No evidence they exist in the layout or pages; missing canonicals risk duplicate content signals even with a small site."
    },
    {
      "title": "Open Graph and Twitter Card meta likely absent",
      "category": "seo_ai",
      "severity": "high",
      "must_fix_before_sprint_2": true,
      "description": "Round 3 GLM finding required complete OG and Twitter meta. Inventory does not confirm they are rendered; without them social sharing previews will break, undermining any phased launch."
    },
    {
      "title": "hreflang implementation unverified",
      "category": "seo_ai",
      "severity": "medium",
      "must_fix_before_sprint_2": false,
      "description": "Layout supposedly includes hreflang tags, but with no evidence of proper en-US/es-US/x-default links, and only a single page, it's unverified. Should be audited and possibly tested before Sprint 2 to avoid cascading errors."
    },
    {
      "title": "C9 pull_gsc.py stub not created",
      "category": "operations",
      "severity": "low",
      "must_fix_before_sprint_2": false,
      "description": "Mandated stub for Performance feedback loop scripts was not created this sprint. Not a blocker but a deviation from the plan; should be created in Sprint 2."
    }
  ],
  "compliments": [
    "The Cloudflare Workers + OpenNext deployment pipeline was executed cleanly, and the debugging of recursive builds and edge runtime issues was thorough—this burned down significant platform risk.",
    "AI‑crawler readiness is excellent with llms.txt, robots.txt that whitelists all major crawlers, and a working /api/llm-context endpoint—this sets a strong foundation for LLM discoverability."
  ],
  "verdict": "revise",
  "verdict_reason": "Sprint 1 laid a solid infrastructure backbone, but the missing SEO fundamentals (llms-full.txt, JSON‑LD, canonical, OG/Twitter tags) constitute critical non‑compliance with locked ADRs; these must be corrected before Sprint 2 begins to avoid compounding debt."
}
